  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "After playing your game for a while, I understood perfectly well why the game would work alot better in VR. I had accepted that and I had planned to continue playing until I had the opportunity to get VR. However, there is one design choice that I thought was particularly odd, but I had no reason to address it. Until now. One thing that has stuck me as odd was that there is no way to move around the hands without VR. Which didn't quite make sense to me, because there are alot of buttons you leave completely untouched on a keyboard. I was fine with this until I had found a model that had the intention of being used by moving around the hands. I would like to request the ability to move the hands on desktop, as there are very easy ways it can be done without interfering with any other keystrokes. Such buttons as Ctrl and Alt are not used in-game. (Although Ctrl is used for a few keystrokes, I don't see the problem with it, as shift allows sprinting and yet that is also used in a few keystrokes.) I chose these buttons is particular because they have two buttons on the right and left, in theory this would allow us to use both hands individually. What I believed could be done, is upon holding the button, the hand is held up wherever the camera is looking, then have the hand brought back down to the player's side upon release. I hope that this can get done, as it would preferably make controlling things a little less of a hassle without VR.",
